{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793807135,"nonce":"s7lwOCRujbAcfRZ9VvwNTjDuJXQ=","title":"Keep code selection captured across inline actions and editor boundaries","message":"A local CodeEditor regression passes repeated forward/backward selection without document synchronization, but fails when the drag crosses an inline action toolbar. Its pointermove handler stops propagation, so the editor stops extending selection. CodeEditor must capture its own selection drag through release.\n\nCover repeated directions, read-only text, inline action crossing, leaving/reentering the editor, release outside the viewport, and a subsequent drag. Assert no action or document transaction runs during selection.\n\nRayDE tracker: 311d7f5feb22349b1054cf41a5a8aa8abf9eaf7589e846f879a2aad6dfe3b985","files":null}]}